; =====================================================================
; cose-hash-structures.cddl
;
; VERBATIM.  These are RFC 9054's own two CDDL fragments, copied
; unchanged, including the source's left margin AND INCLUDING THE `#`
; COMMENT MARKERS THAT ERRATUM 7335 REPORTS AS WRONG.  They were NOT
; authored by this project.  Do not edit, correct or reformat them; the
; repair lives in cose-hash.derived.cddl beside this file, and the
; mechanical consequence of not repairing them is in
; cddl-parse.derived.txt.
;
; THE DOCUMENT CALLS BOTH OF THESE EXAMPLES, not definitions.  Section 2.1
; introduces the first with "An example of a structure that permits all
; of the above fields to exist would look like the following:" and the
; second with "Below is an alternative structure that could be used".
; Neither is normative and neither is registered anywhere.
;
; Source: RFC 9054 section 2.1 of .cache/rfc-9054.txt
;   COSE_Hash_V     lines 211-216, region sha256
;     42d941107b786dc13fa0b8fb4a82249ddd271e36e9671677a487c324073f4176
;   COSE_Hash_Find  lines 224-227, region sha256
;     e55f6c1da8cfcaeb8ca4de6947aaaa0d68b199b90810084a9984a09ccefac1ef
;   cached source sha256
;     75a6bf62b4226baa1e14ccdcc4c603b8a039084ad79677db029e0bbec4525e6f
;
; ERRATUM 7335, status Reported, Technical, section 2.1, reported by Carsten
; Bormann on 2023-02-06, checked at
; https://errata.rfc-editor.org/search/?rfc_number=9054 on 2026-10-20:
; "The comment character for CDDL is a ";", not a "#"."  RFC 8610
; Appendix B gives `COMMENT = ";" *PCHAR CRLF`, and `#` is the TAG
; operator (`type2 = "#" "6" ["." uint] "(" S type S ")" / "#" DIGIT
; ["." uint] / "#"`).  This library holds that grammar verbatim at
; records/ietf/rfc-8610/distilled/schema/cddl.abnf.
;
; WHAT THAT DOES, MEASURED FOR THIS PASS AND NOT GUESSED: the first
; fragment STILL PARSES.  It parses as a group of 24 entries instead of
; 4, because each `#` is read as the "any" type and each comment word
; after it as a bare type reference.  See cddl-parse.derived.txt for the
; entry-by-entry listing.  The second fragment parses as intended.
; =====================================================================

; --- RFC 9054 section 2.1, source lines 211-216 (COSE_Hash_V, as printed)

   COSE_Hash_V = (
       1 : int / tstr, # Algorithm identifier
       2 : bstr, # Hash value
       ? 3 : tstr, # Location of object that was hashed
       ? 4 : any   # object containing other details and things
       )

; --- RFC 9054 section 2.1, source lines 224-227 (COSE_Hash_Find, as printed)

   COSE_Hash_Find = [
       hashAlg : int / tstr,
       hashValue : bstr
   ]
